      "figure": "fig-56",
      "original": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/d9b1/lemmadeck/ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/fig-56.png",
      "inventory": "One wide rectangular coordinate lattice, not separate panels: 36 columns by 12 rows. The vertical axis is 24 columns from the left boundary; the horizontal axis is seven rows below the top. One grid cell represents one coordinate unit. The visible frame therefore spans x=-24..12 and y=-5..7. Positive x/y axes have arrowheads. The x labels are -4,-2,0,2,4; the y labels are 2,4,-2,-4. Three solid straight traces share this frame: a increases steeply from near (-4,-5) to the upper boundary near x=3; b decreases steeply from near x=-2.5 at the upper boundary to near x=3.5 at the lower boundary; c decreases gently from the left boundary near y=3 to the lower boundary near x=8. Traces a and b meet on the vertical axis near y=2. Trace b meets c near (3,-4). Trace c crosses the vertical axis near -3 and the horizontal axis near -12. The labels a, b, and c identify their respective traces. No equations or explicit solved coordinate pairs appear.",
      "uncertainty": "The scanned stroke is thick and skewed. Exact rational endpoints for trace a are not independently readable to sub-cell precision; its frame contacts and axis crossing are observed before comparing the deterministic candidate.",
      "comparisonResolution": "Frozen exercise 848 supplies the exact slopes and intercepts. In particular, a is constructed from y=1.5x+2, giving frame contacts (-14/3,-5) and (10/3,7). These exact fractions are mathematical consequences of the authoritative prose and common frame, not claimed pixel measurements. The scan's approximate contacts do not override that prose."
    },
    {
      "figure": "fig-57",
      "original": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/d9b1/lemmadeck/ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/fig-57.png",
      "inventory": "One wide shared coordinate lattice, 36 columns by 12 rows, with its vertical axis 11 columns from the left and horizontal axis seven rows below the top. One cell is one coordinate unit: x=-11..25, y=-5..7. Arrowheads indicate positive x and y. The x numerals are -4,-2,0,2,4,6,8,10; the y numerals are 4,2,-2,-4. Solid trace a rises shallowly from approximately (-11,-4.2), through (0,-2) and (10,0), to (25,3). Solid trace b falls steeply from approximately (-3,7), through (0,1), to (3,-5). Their intersection is a little right of x=1 and slightly above y=-2. Label a is at the far-right trace; label b is near the upper-left descending trace. In the original, y=-2 is immediately left of the vertical axis. There are no printed equations or solved coordinate pairs."
    },
    {
      "figure": "fig-58",
      "original": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/d9b1/lemmadeck/ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/7a/figures/fig-58.png",
      "inventory": "One tall shared coordinate lattice with half-unit cells, 18 columns by 40 rows: x=-4.5..4.5, y=-2.5..17.5. The vertical axis is central and the horizontal axis lies near the bottom. Visible x numerals are -4,-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3; positive y numerals run 1..16 and negative y numerals are -1,-2. A solid upward-opening parabola labeled y=x^2 has vertex at the origin. A solid falling line labeled y=8-2x passes through (0,8) and (4,0). Their intersections are A=(-4,16) on the left and B=(2,4) on the right; labels A/B sit next to those intersections. Dashed projections connect each intersection to its x and y axes: A to (-4,0)/(0,16), B to (2,0)/(0,4). The curves continue only within the same framed lattice. The scan contains a Cyrillic figure caption, but the mathematical labels themselves are conventional symbols.",
      "uncertainty": "Some horizontal projection strokes coincide with the dark grid in the scan; the vertical dashed projections are independently clear.",
      "comparisonResolution": "The provisional inventory overcalled horizontal projections: only the two vertical guides have independently distinguishable dashed strokes; the horizontal rows at 16 and 4 are continuous lattice lines, not confirmed extra dashed objects. The raw cropped PNG also has no visible figure caption, so the provisional Cyrillic-caption statement is withdrawn. Neither a missing horizontal guide nor cultural caption leakage is a substantiated finding. This correction used the retained original observation, with no reopen."
    }
  ],
